(6219721, 919182, 108069, '<td valign="top">Wow, an actual shape. And a nice one at that. I''ve taken this photo before when in Rome, but not this well.<br/> <br/>No offense, but I''ve had it with this challenge. It makes no sense to me. People have submitted all kinds of crap. This is an actual shape and this should win. 10</td>', 'Wow, an actual shape. And a nice one at that. I''ve taken this photo before when in Rome, but not this well. No offense, but I''ve had it with this challenge. It makes no sense to me. People have submitted all kinds of crap. This is an actual shape and this should win. 10', '2010-11-11 07:55:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6219722, 919187, 108069, '<td valign="top">Sensational photo and I''ll give you high marks. But I will take you to task for this: NUMPTY, why did you not save this for the free study this month? It''s incredible. The detail and even the bird that cooperated, incredible. And you''ve blown it in a "shapes" challenge? You know this will get slaughtered in a shapes challenge, because it is not an actual <i>shape</i>. A rock is not a shape. It is a shape, certainly, but not <i>rock</i>-shaped. There is no rock shape.<br/> <br/>I''ve never taken a photo this good, but if I had, and I entered it, I would have called it the tendrils of the tide or something; something that made me relate to the shapes in front of me. But as it is it''s just a crazy awesome photo, with little to relate to a shape. I just hope you took another from a slightly different angle so you can use it in the November free study.<br/> <br/>I give you 20 for the outlandishly good photo and a huge -13 for trying to squeeze this one into this challenge.<br/> <br/>Would have been a flat 10 had it anything to do with the challenge.<br/> <br/>And +2 for my rant: 9<br/> <br/>10 if it''s in the free study.</td>', 'Sensational photo and I''ll give you high marks. But I will take you to task for this: NUMPTY, why did you not save this for the free study this month? It''s incredible. The detail and even the bird that cooperated, incredible. And you''ve blown it in a "shapes" challenge? You know this will get slaughtered in a shapes challenge, because it is not an actual shape. A rock is not a shape. It is a shape, certainly, but not rock-shaped. There is no rock shape. I''ve never taken a photo this good, but if I had, and I entered it, I would have called it the tendrils of the tide or something; something that made me relate to the shapes in front of me. But as it is it''s just a crazy awesome photo, with little to relate to a shape. I just hope you took another from a slightly different angle so you can use it in the November free study. I give you 20 for the outlandishly good photo and a huge -13 for trying to squeeze this one into this challenge. Would have been a flat 10 had it anything to do with the challenge. And +2 for my rant: 9 10 if it''s in the free study.', '2010-11-11 07:56:37.000000', NULL, 1),
