(6230413, 918213, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This is an interesting abstract of light play that creates an interesting view of contrast and texture.  In the true sense of the term, texture is defined by shape, but I believe the lack of definitive shape outside the realm of the abstract was the undoing of this photo in terms of the challenge.  <br/> <br/>I do, however, love your approach to this topic.  My personal philosophy in photography is to study the specific elements of any particular subject that make it interesting and focus on them instead of the object/subject as a whole.  You will find this path quite rewarding in the personal aspects of this hobby, but not so much in the public aspect as shown by the results of the collective vote on this website :)<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) This is an interesting abstract of light play that creates an interesting view of contrast and texture.  In the true sense of the term, texture is defined by shape, but I believe the lack of definitive shape outside the realm of the abstract was the undoing of this photo in terms of the challenge.   I do, however, love your approach to this topic.  My personal philosophy in photography is to study the specific elements of any particular subject that make it interesting and focus on them instead of the object/subject as a whole.  You will find this path quite rewarding in the personal aspects of this hobby, but not so much in the public aspect as shown by the results of the collective vote on this website :) Keep up the good work :) ', '2010-11-22 21:41:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230430, 918213, 115671, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jmsetzler:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This is an interesting abstract of light play that creates an interesting view of contrast and texture.  In the true sense of the term, texture is defined by shape, but I believe the lack of definitive shape outside the realm of the abstract was the undoing of this photo in terms of the challenge.  <br/> <br/>I do, however, love your approach to this topic.  My personal philosophy in photography is to study the specific elements of any particular subject that make it interesting and focus on them instead of the object/subject as a whole.  You will find this path quite rewarding in the personal aspects of this hobby, but not so much in the public aspect as shown by the results of the collective vote on this website :)<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you kindly for the time you took to comment on my photo. I''m glad to hear that i didn''t DNMC despite the low average vote. I knew that abstracts don''t rate too well, and was really hoping to hear comments like this rather than to get high scores :)</td>', 'Originally posted by jmsetzler: Greetings from the Critique Club :) This is an interesting abstract of light play that creates an interesting view of contrast and texture.  In the true sense of the term, texture is defined by shape, but I believe the lack of definitive shape outside the realm of the abstract was the undoing of this photo in terms of the challenge.   I do, however, love your approach to this topic.  My personal philosophy in photography is to study the specific elements of any particular subject that make it interesting and focus on them instead of the object/subject as a whole.  You will find this path quite rewarding in the personal aspects of this hobby, but not so much in the public aspect as shown by the results of the collective vote on this website :) Keep up the good work :)   Thank you kindly for the time you took to comment on my photo. I''m glad to hear that i didn''t DNMC despite the low average vote. I knew that abstracts don''t rate too well, and was really hoping to hear comments like this rather than to get high scores :)', '2010-11-22 21:49:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230865, 918031, 65319, '<td valign="top">Although this image is presented as dark and broody...I find a quirk of humor in the very idea of this image. But, then again, I have an odd sense of humor. Straight into my FAVS!</td>', 'Although this image is presented as dark and broody...I find a quirk of humor in the very idea of this image. But, then again, I have an odd sense of humor. Straight into my FAVS!', '2010-11-23 10:11:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230883, 919182, 103048, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful! I''d love to know how you manage to get such extraordinary level of sharpness... usually when I try to sharpen my images, I end up getting some noise...</td>', 'This is beautiful! I''d love to know how you manage to get such extraordinary level of sharpness... usually when I try to sharpen my images, I end up getting some noise...', '2010-11-23 10:56:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230921, 919182, 112972, '<td valign="top">Thanks!  I shot this with a wide angle lens all the way zoomed out to 16mm.  The aperture was at f/8.  You get more depth of field with wider angles and of couse at 16mm with an aperture setting of f/8, you should pretty much be able to get great sharpness throughout your image.  The shutter speed wasn''t that great, only at 1/60 sec, but I have pretty steady hands so it wasn''t a problem.  As for sharpening in post, I sharpened the image first, then ran it through noise ninja to reduce the noise a little bit.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by manavg:</b></div><hr/><i> This is beautiful! I''d love to know how you manage to get such extraordinary level of sharpness... usually when I try to sharpen my images, I end up getting some noise... </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-11-23 12:09:06.</i></td>', 'Thanks!  I shot this with a wide angle lens all the way zoomed out to 16mm.  The aperture was at f/8.  You get more depth of field with wider angles and of couse at 16mm with an aperture setting of f/8, you should pretty much be able to get great sharpness throughout your image.  The shutter speed wasn''t that great, only at 1/60 sec, but I have pretty steady hands so it wasn''t a problem.  As for sharpening in post, I sharpened the image first, then ran it through noise ninja to reduce the noise a little bit. Originally posted by manavg: This is beautiful! I''d love to know how you manage to get such extraordinary level of sharpness... usually when I try to sharpen my images, I end up getting some noise... ', '2010-11-23 12:08:02.000000', '2010-11-23 12:09:06.000000', 0),
(6231068, 919165, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>This image, at all levels, embodies the theme of the challenge very well.  After reading your setup info, I think you did an excellent job with what you had to work with.  Maintaining a sense of three dimensions within this composition also adds a lot to the theme.  I can''t really offer you a suggestion for improvement on this idea.  I like the way you executed this one.  Simplicity is often the best solution, and this image answers that call quite nicely... good work!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... This image, at all levels, embodies the theme of the challenge very well.  After reading your setup info, I think you did an excellent job with what you had to work with.  Maintaining a sense of three dimensions within this composition also adds a lot to the theme.  I can''t really offer you a suggestion for improvement on this idea.  I like the way you executed this one.  Simplicity is often the best solution, and this image answers that call quite nicely... good work!', '2010-11-23 15:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6231364, 918768, 86447, '<td valign="top">Lovely shapes ! Perfect for the challenge.</td>', 'Lovely shapes ! Perfect for the challenge.', '2010-11-23 21:36:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6231866, 918031, 99263, '<td valign="top">This grabs me. Wonderful. The mood you created with this image fits the title perfectly.<br/>Ps. Came back for a 2nd look as the words and the song "Horse Latitudes" by The Doors just came to mind. You are probably familiar with The Doors and the song. If not Google "Horse Latitudes"<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-11-24 05:34:38.</i></td>', 'This grabs me. Wonderful. The mood you created with this image fits the title perfectly.Ps. Came back for a 2nd look as the words and the song "Horse Latitudes" by The Doors just came to mind. You are probably familiar with The Doors and the song. If not Google "Horse Latitudes"', '2010-11-24 05:28:12.000000', '2010-11-24 05:34:38.000000', 0),
